(A buffer a function returns is the caller's own. One named by a parameter
 or held by a global is handed back as a copy, so growing or freeing the
 result leaves the original alone; one the function made is handed back as
 it is.)
a buffer called kept is "xy".
To 'give back' with a buffer called data.
    Return a buffer, data.

To 'give kept'.
    Return a buffer, kept.

To 'make one'.
    a buffer called fresh is "new".
    Return a buffer, fresh.

a buffer called hold is "ab".
a buffer called other is 'give back' of hold.
For each number from 1 to 3000, append "abcdefgh" to other.
Print "other {other's size}".
Print "hold {hold's size}".
a buffer called spare is 'give kept'.
Free spare.
Print "kept {kept}".
a buffer called made is 'make one'.
append "er" to made.
Print "made {made}".
